        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fa9fb164-473c-5038-b55a-3030c49debd7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Satoshi Kon, Yasutaka Tsutsui\n- Works: Paprika, Paranoia Agent\n- Organizations: Japanese Animation Creators Association (JAniCA)\n- Places: Sapporo, Hokkaidō\n- Topics: anime film, science fiction, dream therapy\n\nFacts:\n- Yasutaka Tsutsui published the novel Paprika in 1993.\n- Paprika is a 2006 Japanese science-fiction anime film co-written and directed by Satoshi Kon.\n- Paprika is based on Yasutaka Tsutsui's 1993 novel of the same name.\n- Paprika is about a research psychologist who uses a device that lets therapists enter patients' dreams to help them.\n- Satoshi Kon was born on October 12, 1963, in Sapporo, Hokkaidō.\n- Satoshi Kon was a Japanese film director, animator, screenwriter, and manga artist.\n- Satoshi Kon was a member of the Japanese Animation Creators Association (JAniCA).\n- Satoshi Kon was sometimes credited as Yoshihiro Wanibuchi in the credits of Paranoia Agent.\n- Satoshi Kon died on August 24, 2010.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
